  "question": {
    "text": "Let the eccentricity of an ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>b</mi></math>, be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. If this ellipse passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cgS4l",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>29</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
